  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p32-q5a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find $a$ and $b$ for which\n$$\\frac{1}{n(n+3)}=\\frac{a}{n}+\\frac{b}{n+3}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=\\frac13$, $b=-\\frac13$.",
          "worked": "Clearing denominators gives the polynomial identity\n$$\\begin{align*}1&=a(n+3)+bn\\\\1&=(a+b)n+3a.\\end{align*}$$\nSetting $n=0$ gives $1=3a$, so $a=\\frac13$. Setting $n=-3$ gives $1=-3b$, so $b=-\\frac13$.\nTherefore,\n$$\\frac{1}{n(n+3)}=\\frac13\\left(\\frac1n-\\frac1{n+3}\\right).$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q5b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, simplify the sum\n$$\\frac{1}{1\\cdot4}+\\frac{1}{4\\cdot7}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{n\\cdot(n+3)}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{n+2}{3(n+3)}$.\n\nUse part (a); consecutive negative and positive fractions cancel.",
          "worked": "Let $S$ denote the required sum. Using part (a),\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\frac13\\left(1-\\frac14\\right)+\\frac13\\left(\\frac14-\\frac17\\right)+\\cdots+\\frac13\\left(\\frac1n-\\frac1{n+3}\\right)\\\\S&=\\frac13\\left(1-\\frac1{n+3}\\right)\\\\S&=\\frac{n+2}{3(n+3)}.\\end{align*}$$\nAll intermediate fractions cancel.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 47
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q5c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, evaluate\n$$\\frac{1}{1\\cdot4}+\\frac{1}{4\\cdot7}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{97\\cdot100}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{33}{100}$.",
          "worked": "Substitute $n=97$ into the result from part (b):\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\frac{97+2}{3(97+3)}\\\\S&=\\frac{99}{300}\\\\S&=\\frac{33}{100}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      }
    ]
  },
